# core.autocrlf is true in this repo. Git's binary heuristic only looks for NUL
# bytes in the first 8000 bytes, and some files (the bug-report PDFs, for one)
# have a long ASCII header before their first binary stream — so git classifies
# them as text and rewrites their line endings on checkout, corrupting them.
# Declare the binary types explicitly.
#
# No `text=auto` line here on purpose: source files keep the existing autocrlf
# behaviour (CRLF in the working tree, LF in the object store) unchanged.

*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.wav  binary
*.xlsx binary
